==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
Because all of the main threats spawn on a timer, and Doge Dark has a considerable cash drop, you can easily rush the stage by sending out [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]] and [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Talented Can Can]] to collect enough cash from the first Doge Dark to send out [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] to destroy the base.

==='''Chapter 2'''===
It is recommended to collect all of the [[Anti-Starred Alien Treasures]] from Cats of the Cosmos Chapter 3, since the Star Peng would otherwise have stats far too high to be taken on effectively.
Use [[Talents|Talented]] [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] to kill the initial Doge Darks and Wild Doges, and then send out [[Welterweight Cat (Rare Cat)|Ectoweight Cat]] and [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]], preferably with her [[Savage Blow]] talent unlocked, to control the Li'l Zyclone. Once you have clear sights on the enemy base, it's best to rush it with Talented [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] and finish things quickly.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
This stage can be easily rushed down using [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]. You can use Can Can Cat with the Extra Money Talent or [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]] to kill the Doge Dark at the beginning, then you should have enough cash to deploy Awakened Bahamut.

